@ 36.3.2.2.3 - Proto-rGyalrongic to Pati
# citation: Pogostick Man, from Nagano, Yashuiki (1979), “A Historical Study of rGyarong Initials and Prefixes”. Linguistics of the Tibeto-Burman Area 4(2):44 – 68; and Nagano, Yashuiki (1979), “A Historical Study of rGyarong Rhymes”. Linguistics of the Tibeto-Burman Area 5(1):37 – 47 NB: These changes are likely very incomplete. The source did not have much to say about this language. Initials: Rhymes:
	d > l
	{ t͡s, d͡ʒ, NTS } > { {s,t͡ʃ.}, t͡ʃ., m }
	s > ʃ / _n
	n > ∅ / a_
	{ im, it, ik, is, ij } > { em, u, e, es, e }
	uk > o